  "rationale": "A wide turn over a short rise breaks into pieces: radius 4 over a rise of 2 gives 24 blocks in 2 pieces. The sample count comes from the total length of the helix, hypot(arc, rise), and is rounded rather than ceilinged - so 25 samples cover a length of 25.2 and each step moves 1.008 blocks. Since the coordinates are rounded per axis, a step just over one block can land two away: 0.4999 rounds to 0 while 1.5001 rounds to 2. Taking the ceiling keeps every step under a block. Found by a property test, not by a fixed case - the two helix cases already in the suite happen to be steep enough to stay in one piece, which is exactly why the fixed cases missed it.",
